body:
I get failures from the test test_raise_warning_for_operation_with_generic_unit in numpy/_core/tests/test_deprecations.py.  The output for a run of spin test is below, but the problematic behavior is the generation of two warnings in the following:
In [1]: value0 = np.timedelta64(3, 's')

In [2]: np.subtract(value0, 5)
<ipython-input-2-2e78d8f95a84>:1: DeprecationWarning: The 'generic' unit for NumPy timedelta is deprecated, and will raise an error in the future. Please convert the integer with an explicit unit.
  np.subtract(value0, 5)
<ipython-input-2-2e78d8f95a84>:1: DeprecationWarning: The 'generic' unit for NumPy timedelta is deprecated, and will raise an error in the future. This includes implicit conversion of bare integers (e.g. `+ 1`).Please use a specific unit instead.
  np.subtract(value0, 5)
Out[2]: np.timedelta64(-2,'s')

Here's a run of all the tests in test_deprecation.py that shows 8 failures.  Strangely, I get only two of these failures when I run the full test suite with spin test -m full -j 12.


